{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uzn3gltjswqj74bjwwz72ourz6pgrkx4qqgqy5k46imqfvd6px6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Diagnosis: LLVM commuted the `a.y * b.y` multiply (`mulss` dst = `b.y` instead of `a.y`), so when *both* y-operands are NaN the propagated payload differs. Let me reproduce the hardware propagation order explicitly in portable safe Rust:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":35616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":915,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da1a2aec-6f74-4e8a-9ca4-4e4078bb73b9","uuid":"492a8f7d-a810-49ea-8b28-03fbf9dab300","timestamp":"2026-08-26T19:41:13.916Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uzn3gltjswqj74bjwwz72ourz6pgrkx4qqgqy5k46imqfvd6px6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_014yZNV2GgNecNnKo1jSp7L3","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-9Lbuqb/translation/src/lib.rs","old_string":"/// ```c\n/// float c2Dot(c2v a, c2v b) { return a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y; }\n/// ```\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub extern \"C\" fn c2Dot(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> f32 {\n    a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y\n}","new_string":"/// Quiet a NaN the way an x86 SSE arithmetic instruction does: the sign bit and\n/// payload are preserved and the \"quiet\" mantissa bit (bit 22) is forced on, so\n/// an sNaN such as `0x7f800001` becomes `0x7fc00001`.\n#[inline]\nfn quiet_nan(v: f32) -> f32 {\n    f32::from_bits(v.to_bits() | 0x0040_0000)\n}\n\n/// `mulss dst, src` — an IEEE multiply with x86's *operand-ordered* NaN\n/// propagation: if the destination operand is a NaN it wins, otherwise the\n/// source operand's NaN wins, otherwise the ordinary product (which yields the\n/// default qNaN `0x7fc00000` for the invalid `0 * inf` case).\n///\n/// This is spelled out explicitly because C's `a.x * b.x` is compiled by gcc to\n/// `mulss` with `a.x` as the destination, and therefore propagates `a`'s NaN\n/// when *both* operands are NaNs with different payloads. LLVM considers `fmul`\n/// commutative and freely swaps the operands (it emits `mulss` with `b.y` as the\n/// destination), which would propagate the other payload. Handling the NaN cases\n/// by hand pins the observable bit pattern to the C library's.\n#[inline]\nfn mulss(dst: f32, src: f32) -> f32 {\n    if dst.is_nan() {\n        quiet_nan(dst)\n    } else if src.is_nan() {\n        quiet_nan(src)\n    } else {\n        dst * src\n    }\n}\n\n/// `addss dst, src` — an IEEE add with x86's operand-ordered NaN propagation\n/// (see [`mulss`]). The non-NaN path still produces the default qNaN for the\n/// invalid `inf + (-inf)` case.\n#[inline]\nfn addss(dst: f32, src: f32) -> f32 {\n    if dst.is_nan() {\n        quiet_nan(dst)\n    } else if src.is_nan() {\n        quiet_nan(src)\n    } else {\n        dst + src\n    }\n}\n\n/// ```c\n/// float c2Dot(c2v a, c2v b) { return a.x * b.x + a.y * b.y; }\n/// ```\n///\n/// gcc lowers this to\n/// ```text\n/// mulss b.x, a.x   ; dst = a.x\n/// mulss b.y, a.y   ; dst = a.y\n/// addss y, x       ; dst = a.x*b.x\n/// ```\n/// so the multiplications keep `a`'s component as the destination and the\n/// addition keeps the *x* product as the destination. [`mulss`]/[`addss`]\n/// reproduce that ordering exactly, which only matters for NaN payloads.\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub extern \"C\" fn c2Dot(a: c2v, b: c2v) -> f32 {\n    addss(mulss(a.x, b.x), mulss(a.y, b.y))\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":35616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":915,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da1a2aec-6f74-4e8a-9ca4-4e4078bb73b9","uuid":"4a89846c-53ae-4ceb-841e-19c9a830ed8b","timestamp":"2026-08-26T19:41:26.921Z"}
